> knn machine learning explain with example

● K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

  What is KNN?

  KNN is a simple ML algorithm that classifies a new data point based on the majority class of its K nearest neighbors.

  ▎ "Tell me who your neighbors are, and I'll tell you who you are."

  ---
  How it Works

  1. Choose a value of K (e.g., K=3)
  2. Calculate distance from the new point to all existing points
  3. Pick the K closest points
  4. Vote — the majority class wins

  ---
  Simple Example: Classifying a Fruit 🍎🍊

  ┌───────┬────────────┬─────────────┬────────┐
  │ Fruit │ Weight (g) │ Color Score │ Label  │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ A     │ 150        │ 8           │ Apple  │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ B     │ 160        │ 7           │ Apple  │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ C     │ 130        │ 9           │ Apple  │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ D     │ 200        │ 3           │ Orange │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ E     │ 210        │ 2           │ Orange │
  ├───────┼────────────┼─────────────┼────────┤
  │ ?     │ 155        │ 8           │ ???    │
  └───────┴────────────┴─────────────┴────────┘

  Step 1: Calculate distances from ? (155, 8) to each fruit using Euclidean distance:
  Distance = √((x2-x1)² + (y2-y1)²)

  A: √((155-150)² + (8-8)²) = √25       = 5.0  ✅
  B: √((155-160)² + (8-7)²) = √26       = 5.1  ✅
  C: √((155-130)² + (8-9)²) = √626      = 25.0
  D: √((155-200)² + (8-3)²) = √2050     = 45.3
  E: √((155-210)² + (8-2)²) = √3061     = 55.3

